  nonce: a557  # a557
  data:  # a557
    kind: invariant  # a557
    title: "A test's id must not depend on when it was collected: a time-stamped parameter stops every parallel run whose workers import the file in different seconds"  # a557
    status: violated  # a557
    priority: 2  # a557
    parent:  # a557
    tags:  # a557
    - ci_infrastructure  # a557
    - testing  # a557
    - trunk_green  # a557
    isbefore: []  # a557
    duplicate_of: []  # a557
    not_duplicate_of: []  # a557
    pr_ref:  # a557
    description: "FOUND 2026-11-17 on PR #2223 (the per-PR gate, 1,478 selected files, -n 8): pytest stopped at collection with \"Different tests were collected between gw7 and gw6\" and ran nothing (1 skipped, 2 errors in 182 s).\n\nCAUSE. tests/test_cron_status_nudge.py (added in PR #2219) parametrized a test with `json.dumps({**verdict(), ...})`, and `verdict()` stamps `finished_at` from `time.time()`. The value is made while the module is imported and becomes part of the test's id, so two xdist workers that import the module in different seconds collect different ids (\"...finished_at\": \"2026-11-17T08:52:11Z\"... against ...12Z). Whether a run fails depends on whether the workers straddle a second boundary; the local pre-PR runs (-n 3) and the CI runs of #2219 and #2220 did not.\n\nFIXED IN THE SAME PR (#2223, its own commit): the good verdict is built inside the test; the parameters are fixed names.\n\nSWEEP, BY BEHAVIOUR NOT BY GREP (the value came through a helper, which a grep for time.time() in a decorator does not see): every test file of the whole-suite manifest collected twice, 69 s apart, with `smart-test <files> --collect-only -q --no-cov -n 0`, and the two sorted id lists compared. 40,985 ids each, 0 differ. Control: the same comparison on the unfixed file gives 2 differing ids of 44. Lists: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/collect_ids/.\n\nWHAT THE SWEEP DOES NOT SHOW. An id that depends on the DATE, the hour, the host, the process id or an environment variable: two collections 69 s apart on one machine agree on all of those. Not checked.\n\nNO GUARD EXISTS. xdist is the only detector, and only when two workers disagree. A cheap one: a collection hook in the root conftest.py that fails when a test id contains the current date or the current epoch second's leading digits."  # a557
    fields:  # a557
      statement: "Collecting the suite twice, at different times, gives the same test ids."  # a557
      root_cause: "A parametrize argument computed at import from the clock (through a helper), so each xdist worker makes its own value; nothing checks ids for a collection-time value."  # a557
